  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1966-p17.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "From the first equation, \\(x^2=1-4y^2.\\) Substitution into the second gives \\[ 4(1-4y^2)+y^2=4, \\] so \\(y=0.\\) Then \\(x^2=1,\\) giving the two points \\((1,0)\\) and \\((-1,0).\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Use the first equation to substitute for \\(x^2\\) in the second",
        "After finding \\(y,\\) count both possible signs of \\(x\\)"
      ],
